lab.build:
Write a negative case, plugins/team-notes/evals/stays-quiet-on-goodbye/, the shape of Dana's missing case: the prompt asks for a short goodbye post for Dana, who leaves the team on Friday. Give it two graders: does-not-fire, a tool_used grader on Skill whose input_match names welcome-note, with min 0, max 0 and arm: both; and says-goodbye, a regex that finds goodbye, farewell, last day or miss you, ignoring case. Save these recorded runs as recorded/stays-quiet-on-goodbye.json and score them with node score.mjs plugins/team-notes/evals/stays-quiet-on-goodbye recorded/stays-quiet-on-goodbye.json. You should see WITH 0.83, W/OUT 1.00 and Δ -0.17. Say what our plugin CI would do with this result and why.

{
  "case": "stays-quiet-on-goodbye",
  "arms": {
    "with": [
      { "toolCalls": [],
        "lastMessage": "Friday is Dana's last day with us. Thank you for every review and every laugh, Dana. We will miss you!" },
      { "toolCalls": [{ "tool": "Skill", "input": { "skill": "team-notes:welcome-note" } }],
        "lastMessage": "Goodbye and good luck, Dana! Thank you for everything you built with us." },
      { "toolCalls": [],
        "lastMessage": "A farewell to Dana, who leaves on Friday: thank you for three great years on the team." }
    ],
    "without": [
      { "toolCalls": [],
        "lastMessage": "Friday is Dana's last day. Dana, thank you for everything, and keep in touch!" },
      { "toolCalls": [],
        "lastMessage": "Goodbye, Dana! The team will not be the same without you." },
      { "toolCalls": [],
        "lastMessage": "Please join me in a farewell to Dana, who leaves us on Friday." }
    ]
  }
}
